## Discover hostname from IP Address ##

Resolve-DnsName 172.16.68.164


Answer looks like:


Name                           Type   TTL   Section   NameHost
----                           ----   ---   -------   --------
100.1.168.192.in-addr.arpa     PTR    1200  Answer    PC-USER01.company.local


==================================================================================

## From CMD ##

nslookup 192.168.1.100


Answer looks loke

Server:  DC01.company.local
Address: 192.168.1.10

Name:    PC-USER01.company.local
Address: 192.168.1.100

===================================================================================
## Or ##

nbtstat -A 192.168.1.100

Look for the line:

PC-USER01       <00>  UNIQUE  Registered

===================================================================================





